  "space chronicles / reading another world": "太空信笺 / 读懂另一个世界",
  "ON LEARNING TO READ ANOTHER WORLD": "学习阅读另一个世界",
  "How does a mark become something we can read? This atlas connects four approaches: language and attention, a colour experiment, the reorganisation of a familiar script, and parallel inscriptions. ​ Sapir and Whorf frame the relationship between language, culture and habitual interpretation. Linguistic relativity invites us to examine what we attend to; it does not mean that language determines thought. The Russian blues study offers task-specific evidence: a colour-category advantage disappeared under verbal interference. ​ Xu Bing moves from perception to practice. English letters take forms resembling Chinese characters. Textbooks, tracing exercises and a classroom make the unfamiliar arrangement learnable through a visible rule. ​ The Rosetta Stone offers a complementary lesson: parallel versions of a text can provide a reference for interpretation. Its role here is comparison, rather than a model for inventing an alphabet. ​ For Space Chronicles, these cases suggest letting planetary patterns shape distinctive letterforms while retaining a shared correspondence, so a reader on Earth can follow a traveller’s reply.": "一个符号如何成为可读的文字？这份图谱联系了四种路径：语言与注意力、色彩实验、熟悉文字的重组，以及平行铭文。萨丕尔和沃尔夫讨论语言、文化与习惯性理解之间的关系。语言相对论促使我们审视注意的对象，并不意味着语言决定思想。“俄罗斯蓝色”研究提供了特定任务中的证据：色彩分类的识别优势在言语干扰下消失。徐冰将感知转向实践，让英文字母呈现类似汉字的形式。教材、描红与课堂通过可见规则，使陌生的文字组合变得可以学习。罗塞塔石碑提供了另一种启示：同一文本的平行版本能成为解读的参照。它在此用于比较，而非作为发明字母的模型。对《太空信笺》而言，这些案例启发我们以行星纹理塑造独特字形，同时保留共同的对应关系，让地球上的读者能够读懂旅人的回信。",
  "RESEARCH ATLAS": "研究图谱",
  "Routes connect ideas and materials. They do not represent historical causation.": "连线连接观念与材料，不代表历史因果关系。",
  "HIEROGLYPHIC DEMOTIC ANCIENT GREEK": "象形文字 世俗体 古希腊文",
  "One decree Two languages Three scripts": "一份法令 两种语言 三种文字",
  "Illustrative palette": "示意色板",
  "01 LANGUAGE & ATTENTION Sapir and Whorf provide a historical frame for thinking about language and habitual interpretation. Influence is not determination.": "01 语言与注意力 萨丕尔和沃尔夫提供了思考语言与习惯性理解的历史框架。影响并不等于决定。",
  "02 RUSSIAN BLUES / 2007 Winawer et al., PNAS. A colour-category advantage disappeared under verbal interference. This is task-specific evidence. doi:10.1073/pnas.0701644104": "02 俄罗斯蓝色 / 2007 Winawer 等，PNAS。色彩分类的识别优势在言语干扰下消失。这是特定任务中的证据。doi:10.1073/pnas.0701644104",
  "03–06 A SCRIPT THAT CAN BE LEARNED Xu Bing, Square Word Calligraphy, 1994–ongoing. Textbooks, tracing exercises and a classroom make the construction rule visible.": "03–06 可以学习的文字 徐冰，《英文方块字书法》，1994 年至今。教材、描红与课堂使文字构造规则可见。",
  "07–09 MAKING THE READING SYSTEM Woodblock type, plate carving and stone-cut type show the material work behind the new letter arrangement. Artist documentation, xubing.com.": "07–09 制作阅读系统 木活字、刻版与石刻字模展示了新文字排列背后的材料制作过程。艺术家档案：xubing.com。",
  "10 A PARALLEL REFERENCE The Rosetta Stone, 196 BCE. A decree in three scripts helped provide clues for decipherment. British Museum; photograph: H. Hillewaert, CC BY-SA 4.0.": "10 平行参照 罗塞塔石碑，公元前 196 年。以三种文字书写的法令为破译提供了线索。大英博物馆；摄影：H. Hillewaert，CC BY-SA 4.0。",
  "PROJECT INFERENCE Observe a surface → abstract a form → preserve a correspondence. The proposed planetary script is a design exploration, not evidence of future linguistic change.": "项目推导 观察表面 → 提炼形态 → 保留对应关系。拟议的行星文字是一种设计探索，并非未来语言变化的证据。",
  "SOURCE IMAGES / XU BING STUDIO · PNAS · BRITISH MUSEUM COLLECTION": "图片来源 / 徐冰工作室 · PNAS · 大英博物馆馆藏",
  "space chronicles / sending a letter home": "太空信笺 / 寄一封家书",
  "ON SENDING A LETTER HOME": "关于寄一封家书",
  "What survives the journey from one world to another? A letter carries information, but also an address, a memory and an imagined reader. These references approach communication as a relationship sustained across distance. ​ Qiaopi joins family correspondence with remittances. Handwriting and material support keep a bond between people who live apart. It provides a human starting point for the project: what would future travellers want to tell those who remain on Earth? ​ The Voyager Golden Record expands that question to the scale of a planet. Selected sounds and images describe a curated Earth, while instructions on its cover address an unknown reader. Selection and explanation become part of the message. ​ NASA’s HERA ground simulation examines coordination when replies arrive late. Katie Paterson’s Earth–Moon–Earth gives transmission a perceptible form: gaps in a returning signal become pauses in a piano performance. Waiting and loss shape the act of receiving. ​ Together, the cases frame Space Chronicles as a traveller’s reply: a message that carries traces of another place while maintaining a connection with home.": "从一个世界到另一个世界，什么能够留存？一封信承载信息，也承载地址、记忆与想象中的读者。这些参考案例将沟通视为跨越距离而维系的关系。侨批把家书与汇款联系起来，笔迹与物质支持维系着分隔两地的人。它为项目提供了人的出发点：未来的旅人想对留在地球上的人说些什么？旅行者金唱片将这一问题扩展到行星尺度。经过选择的声音与图像描绘了一个被编选的地球，封面说明面向未知的读者。选择与解释也成为信息的一部分。NASA 的 HERA 地面模拟研究了回复延迟时的协作。Katie Paterson 的《地球—月球—地球》让传输变得可感：返回信号中的缺失成为钢琴演奏中的停顿。等待与损失改变了接收的体验。这些案例共同将《太空信笺》定位为旅人的回信：带着异地痕迹，同时保持与家园的联结。",
  "Routes connect research ideas, not signal trajectories. The future reply is a project narrative proposal.": "连线联系研究观念，并非信号轨迹。未来回信是本项目提出的叙事设想。",
  "SEND": "发送",
  "WAIT": "等待",
  "A selected world. An unknown reader.": "一个经过选择的世界。一位未知的读者。",
